  "text": "Maqam Bayati Shuri A member of the Maqam Bayati Family Maqam Index Pronunciation of Bayati Shuri Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play. Maqam Bayati Shuri is a variation of Maqam Bayati with a lowered 5 th degree. It starts with the root Jins Bayati on the tonic followed by Jins Hijaz on the 4 th degree. It is a very popular maqam in its own right, especially in the Muwashahat and Adwar vocal compositions. Explore other maqamat in the Maqam Bayati Family . Watch a 1-minute sample Violin Taqsim in Maqam Bayati Shuri by Sami Abu Shumays. Sama‘i Bayati Shuri Nagham al-Ams Vol. 2 (Bayati Shuri) Taqsim Violin in Maqam Bayati Shuri Nagham al-Ams Vol. 2 (Bayati Shuri) Muwashah Hibbi Da‘ani Lil-Wisal Sabah Fakhri Music by Sayyed Darwish Nagham al-Ams Vol. 2 (Bayati Shuri) Muwashah Talaffata al-Dhabiyu Sabah Fakhri Nagham al-Ams Vol. 2 (Bayati Shuri) Dawr Dayya‘ti Mustaqbal Hayati Music and Vocals by Sayyed Darwish Qadd Ah Ya Hilu Nay Barghouti Qadd Habibi Ghab Muhammad Khayri Taqsim Qanun in Maqam Bayati Shuri Marie Jubran Wasla in Bayati Shuri",
